<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walloon Brabant</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walloon Brabant is a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> in the Walloon Region, created in 1995 when the old province of Brabant was divided. Its capital is Wavre, and its towns include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nivelles">Nivelles</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> and Louvain-la-Neuve, home of the French-speaking UCLouvain. It covers the French-speaking southern part of the medieval Duchy of Brabant.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/walloon-brabant.jpg" alt="Walloon Brabant" width="320" height="284" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moyogo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drapeau_Province_BE_Brabant_Wallon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
